-- title:
--   Torsion-freeness of the level rings over ℤ[1/f]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $A =$ `Afin p` be the integral chart algebra `chartAlgFin` attached to the element `jFull p` inside the field `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $p$. Let $f$ be a nonzero integer divisible by $p$, let $u \in A$, and let $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$. Assume that for every prime $q \neq p$ the ideal of $A$ generated by the image of $q$ is prime, and that for every such $q$ the element $g(u) \in A$, obtained by evaluating $g$ at $u$ over $\mathbb{Z}$, does not lie in that ideal. The conclusion is that the ring
--   $$\mathrm{levelRing}\;p\;f\;u\;g \;=\; A\bigl[1/f\bigr] \big/ \bigl(g(u)\bigr),$$
--   the quotient of the localisation of $A$ away from the image of $f$ by the principal ideal generated by the evaluation of $g$ at the image of $u$, satisfies `NoZeroSMulDivisors` over `Localization.Away f` $= \mathbb{Z}[1/f]$: if $r \in \mathbb{Z}[1/f]$ and $b$ lies in this quotient with $r \cdot b = 0$, then $r = 0$ or $b = 0$.
--
--   This is the torsion-freeness (equivalently, flatness) of a level ring of the finite-$j$ chart of the integral model over the base $\mathbb{Z}[1/f]$, obtained from the primality of $qA$ and the non-vanishing of $g(u)$ modulo $q$ for all primes $q \neq p$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin) in the construction of finite étale covers of the chart.
